From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.ui.xaml: XAML text -- XamlReader.Load, Application.LoadComponent

Pages are made from markup; there was no markup at all. XAML text per the public XAML language documentation: an element is an object -- ours by its name in the presentation namespace, or the application's ("using:" namespaces) through its IXamlMetadataProvider; attributes and property elements set members, strings converted by the member's type (numbers, Auto, Thickness, CornerRadius, GridLength, colours by name or #hex as brushes, enums, font weights, font families); child elements go to the type's content property; Owner.Member is an attached property; x:Name names, x:ConnectionId hands the object to the component being loaded (IComponentConnector). XamlReader.Load reads a string; Application.LoadComponent reads the component's ms-appx: markup from the package's (or program's) folder onto the component. Malformed markup fails with an error: unclosed elements, values of the wrong type, text that is not XML, nesting deeper than 256; unknown elements are skipped. The object writer is shared with the compiled-XAML reader to come. The implementation is ours. Behind the XAML switch of 6131.
---
